`z = j²((-3R²+4R+3)Lg/(72R) + 1/24 - 1/(12R) - 1/(4R²) + 3/(16R³))`,
`p2 = j²((R²-4R+3)Lg/(48R²) - 1/(48R))`.

All three are `C^∞` on `(1, ∞) ⊃ [3, ∞)`; genuine first/second derivatives are computed, and
`EF = EM = EC = 0` and `p2' = -Q u/R² - v1 b1'` are proved on `(1, ∞)` by exact algebra with `Lg` an
